---
import { PLANS, PLAN_ORDER, watchLimit } from '../lib/plans';
---

<section class="workspace-features wrap" aria-label="Workspace features and usage">
  <h2>From a capture to a client deliverable</h2>
  <p>
    Every plan includes private projects, saved batch settings, URL-list and sitemap capture, manual launch review
    status, and before-and-after web reports with expiring links.
  </p>
  <div class="feature-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scroll to compare plan features">
    <table>
      <caption>What each plan includes</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Feature</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <th scope="col">{PLANS[id].name}</th>
          ))}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Screenshots / calendar month</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <td>{PLANS[id].quota.toLocaleString()}</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Source image retention</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <td>{PLANS[id].historyDays} days</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Projects, batches &amp; web reports</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map(() => (
            <td>Included</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Branded PDF reports</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <td>{PLANS[id].formats.includes('pdf') ? 'Included' : '—'}</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Monitor slots</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <td>{watchLimit(id) || '—'}</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">API access</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <td>{PLANS[id].api ? 'Included' : '—'}</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Project collaborators</th>
          {PLAN_ORDER.map((id) => (
            <td>{id === 'business' ? '3 per project' : 'Owner only'}</td>
          ))}
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <article>
      <h3>What uses a screenshot?</h3>
      <p>
        One generated image counts as one screenshot. Desktop + mobile counts as two. Scroll series counts per frame.
        Manual captures, batches, API calls and monitor checks share the same monthly allowance, resetting on the first
        day of each UTC calendar month—even on annual billing.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Monitor slots are not extra quota</h3>
      <p>
        One daily monitor needs about 30 screenshots per 30 days; one hourly monitor needs about 720. For example, 25
        hourly monitors would need about 18,000 screenshots, exceeding Pro’s 2,000 allowance. The app forecasts usage
        before you save a schedule.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Reports and sharing</h3>
      <p>
        Web reports reuse existing captures without using screenshot quota. Paid PDF report exports allow six
        exports/hour and up to 16 MB of source images. Review links expire after 1, 7 or 30 days and can be revoked.
        Downloaded copies cannot be recalled.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Retention and teams</h3>
      <p>
        Reports do not extend source image retention. Missing images become unavailable. Business includes three
        collaborators per project, including pending invitations: viewers read reports and editors can comment. Only the
        owner manages captures, monitors and billing.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p>
    Workspace limits: 100 projects/account, 30 saved settings and 100 reports/project. Batch queues support 25
    screenshots; desktop/mobile launch checks support 12 URLs. Weekly digests are opt-in and sent to each recipient’s
    verified account email.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/sample-report">See an illustrative client report →</a>
  </p>
</section>
<style>
  .workspace-features {
    padding-block: 32px 64px;
  }
  .workspace-features h2 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 38px);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .workspace-features p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 12px 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .feature-table {
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 16px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .feature-table table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 650px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .feature-table th,
  .feature-table td {
    padding: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2);
  }
  .feature-table caption {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .feature-grid article {
    padding: 22px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
</style>
